To understand what a wordlist is, open a plain text file (like Notepad or a .txt file) in your mind. That is literally all it is.

1. What Does a "Wordlist" Look Like Inside?
A wordlist is not fancy code. It is just a massive .txt file containing thousands of words written one after another, each on its own line.

If you opened /usr/share/wordlists/dirbuster/directory-list.txt in a text editor, you would see this:

admin
login
images
uploads
dashboard
secret
test
backup
database
contact
products
... (thousands more words)

Cybersecurity professionals and Linux distributions (like Kali Linux) compile these lists by analyzing millions of real websites to find the most commonly used folder names developers create
